STOTRA = {
    "deity": "kavya",
    "doc_title": "Meghadūta · Pūrvamegha",
    "app_title": "Meghadūta I",
    "h1": "Meghadūta · Pūrvamegha",
    "subtitle": "The Cloud Messenger · Part 1: the Journey (verses 1–66)",
    "note": "Kālidāsa’s lyric of a yakṣa banished for a year from his home and his wife, who asks a rain-cloud to carry his message to her in the far north. This first part is the cloud’s route from Rāmagiri to the Himalaya, in the mandākrāntā metre.",
    "footer": "Source: Sanskrit Wikisource — मेघदूतम् - पूर्वमेघः (public domain); English translation original; editorial notes in SOURCES §10",
    "sections": [
    {'padas': ['kaścitkāntāvirahaguruṇā svādhikārātpramattaḥ', 'śāpenāstaṅgamitamahimā varṣabhogyeṇa bhartuḥ |', 'yakṣaścakre janakatanayāsnānapuṇyodakeṣu', 'snigdhacchāyātaruṣu vasatiṃ rāmagiryāśrameṣu'], 'num': '|| 1 ||', 'gloss': 'A certain yakṣa, careless in his duty, had his power taken from him by his master’s curse — a year’s exile, made heavy by parting from his beloved — and made his dwelling in the hermitages of Rāmagiri, whose waters are hallowed by Sītā’s bathing and whose trees give deep, cool shade. |'},
    {'padas': ['tasminnadrau katicidabalāviprayuktaḥ sa kāmī', 'nītvā māsān kanakavalayabhraṃśariktaprakoṣṭhaḥ |', 'āṣāḍhasya prathamadivase meghamāśliṣṭasānuṃ', 'vaprakrīḍāpariṇatagajaprekṣaṇīyaṃ dadarśa'], 'num': '|| 2 ||', 'gloss': 'Parted from his wife, the lovesick yakṣa spent some months on that mountain, his forearm bare where the gold bracelet had slipped. On the first day of Āṣāḍha he saw a cloud clinging to the peak, lovely as an elephant playing at butting a bank. |'},
    {'padas': ['tasya sthitvā kathamapi puraḥ kautukādhānaheto-', 'rantarbāṣpaściramanucaro rājarājasya dadhyau |', "meghāloke bhavati sukhino'pyanyathāvṛtti cetaḥ", 'kaṇṭhāśleṣapraṇayini jane kiṃ punardūrasaṃsthe'], 'num': '|| 3 ||', 'gloss': 'Standing before it, the servant of the king of kings, somehow holding back his tears, brooded long to rouse his own eagerness. At the sight of a cloud even a happy man’s mind is unsettled; how much more one whose beloved is far away and who longs to hold her. |'},
    {'padas': ['pratyāsanne nabhasi dayitājīvitālambanārthī', 'jīmūtena svakuśalamayīṃ hārayiṣyanpravṛttim |', 'sa pratyagraiḥ kuṭajakusumaiḥ kalpitārghāya tasmai', 'prītaḥ prītipramukhavacanaṃ svāgataṃ vyājahāra'], 'num': '|| 4 ||', 'gloss': 'With the month of rains near, wanting to keep his beloved alive and to send news of his well-being by the cloud, he offered it fresh kuṭaja flowers as a welcome-gift, and gladly greeted it with the loving words of a host. |'},
    {'padas': ['dhūmajyotiḥsalilamarutāṃ saṃnipātaḥ kva meghaḥ', 'sandeśārthāḥ kva paṭukaraṇaiḥ prāṇibhiḥ prāpaṇīyāḥ |', 'ityautsukyādaparigaṇayan guhyakastaṃ yayāce', 'kāmārtā hi prakṛtikṛpaṇāścetanācetaneṣu'], 'num': '|| 5 ||', 'gloss': 'A cloud — a mere meeting of smoke, light, water and wind — and messages that only creatures of keen faculties can carry: how far apart they are! Not weighing this, in his eagerness the yakṣa begged it; for the love-stricken are by nature pitiable, and cannot tell the living from the lifeless. |'},
    {'padas': ['jātaṃ vaṃśe bhuvanavidite puṣkarāvartakānāṃ', 'jānāmi tvāṃ prakṛtipuruṣaṃ kāmarūpaṃ maghonaḥ |', "tenārthitvaṃ tvayi vidhivaśād dūrabandhurgato'haṃ", 'yācñā moghā varamadhiguṇe nādhame labdhakāmā'], 'num': '|| 6 ||', 'gloss': 'I know that you were born in the world-famous line of the Puṣkara and Āvartaka clouds, and that you are Indra’s own minister, taking whatever shape you wish. It is by fate, far from my kin, that I make this request of you: better a plea refused by the noble than one granted by the base. |'},
    {'padas': ['santaptānāṃ tvamasi śaraṇaṃ tatpayoda priyāyāḥ', 'sandeśaṃ me hara dhanapatikrodhaviśleṣitasya |', 'gantavyā te vasatiralakā nāma yakṣeśvarāṇāṃ', 'bāhyodyānasthitaharaśiraścandrikādhautaharmyā'], 'num': '|| 7 ||', 'gloss': 'You are the refuge of the scorched, O cloud; carry my message to my beloved, from me, whom the wrath of the lord of wealth has parted from her. You must go to Alakā, the city of the yakṣa lords, whose palaces are washed by the moonlight from the head of Śiva in its outer garden. |'},
    {'padas': ['tvāmārūḍhaṃ pavanapadavīmudgṛhītālakāntāḥ', 'prekṣiṣyante pathikavanitāḥ pratyayādāśvasantyaḥ |', 'kaḥ sannaddhe virahavidhurāṃ tvayyupekṣeta jāyāṃ', "na syādanyo'pyahamiva jano yaḥ parādhīnavṛttiḥ"], 'num': '|| 8 ||', 'gloss': 'When you have risen onto the path of the wind, travelling women, their hair lifted from their brows, will look up at you and take comfort in hope. When you are gathered, who would neglect a wife who pines in separation — unless, like me, he were another’s servant? |'},
    {'padas': ['tvāṃ cāvaśyaṃ divasagaṇanātatparāmekapatnīm', 'avyāpannāmavihatagatirdrakṣyasi bhrātṛjāyām |', 'āśābandhaḥ kusumasadṛśaṃ prāyaśo hyaṅganānām', 'sadyaḥ pāti praṇayi hṛdayaṃ viprayoge ruṇaddhi'], 'num': '|| 9 ||', 'gloss': 'And you will surely see my wife, your brother’s wife, faithful and still alive, spending her days counting the days till my return. For the bond of hope, like a flower-stalk, holds up the loving hearts of women, which would otherwise at once fall in parting. |'},
    {'padas': ['mandaṃ mandaṃ nudati pavanaścānukūlo yathā tvāṃ', 'vāmaścāyaṃ nadati madhuraṃ cātakaste sagandhaḥ |', 'garbhādhānakṣaṇaparicayānnūnamābaddhamālāḥ', 'seviṣyante nayanasubhagaṃ khe bhavantaṃ balākāḥ'], 'num': '|| 10 ||', 'gloss': 'The favourable wind drives you gently on, and this cātaka, your kinsman, sings sweetly on your left; and cranes, who know the moment of conception, will tie themselves in garlands and wait upon you in the sky, a delight to the eye. |'},
    {'padas': ['kartuṃ yacca prabhavati mahīmucchilīndhrāmavandhyām', 'tacchrutvā te śravaṇasubhagaṃ garjitaṃ mānasotkāḥ |', 'ā kailāsād bisakisalayacchedapātheyavantaḥ', 'sampatsyante nabhasi bhavato rājahaṃsāḥ sahāyāḥ'], 'num': '|| 11 ||', 'gloss': 'And, hearing your thunder, sweet to the ear, which can make the earth fruitful with mushrooms, the royal swans, longing for Lake Mānasa, with lotus-shoot fibres for their journey-food, will be your companions in the sky as far as Kailāsa. |'},
    {'padas': ['āpṛcchasva priyasakhamamuṃ tuṅgamāliṅgya śailam', 'vandyaiḥ puṃsāṃ raghupatipadairaṅkitaṃ mekhalāsu |', 'kāle kāle bhavati bhavato yasya saṃyogametya', 'snehavyaktiściravirahajaṃ muñcato bāṣpamuṣṇam'], 'num': '|| 12 ||', 'gloss': 'Take leave of this dear friend, the lofty mountain, embracing him — his slopes are marked with the footprints of Raghu’s lord, which men revere — who, every time you meet him, shows his love by shedding hot tears born of the long parting. |'},
    {'padas': ['mārgaṃ tāvacchṛṇu kathayatastvatprayāṇānurūpam', 'sandeśaṃ me tadanu jalada śroṣyasi śrotrapeyam |', 'khinnaḥ khinnaḥ śikhariṣu padaṃ nyasya gantāsi yatra', 'kṣīṇaḥ kṣīṇaḥ parilaghu payaḥ srotasāṃ copabhujya'], 'num': '|| 13 ||', 'gloss': 'First hear the road, fitted to your journey, as I tell it; then, cloud, you will hear my message, a drink for the ear. Wherever you go, weary, set your foot on the mountain-tops to rest, and, when you are spent, drink the light water of the streams. |'},
    {'padas': ['adreḥ śṛṅgaṃ harati pavanaḥ kiṃsvidityunmukhībhir-', 'dṛṣṭotsāhaścakitacakitaṃ mugdhasiddhāṅganābhiḥ |', 'sthānādasmāt sarasaniculādutpatodaṅmukhaḥ khaṃ', 'diṅnāgānāṃ pathi pariharan sthūlahastāvalepān'], 'num': '|| 14 ||', 'gloss': '“Is the wind carrying off the mountain’s peak?” — so, with upturned faces, the simple Siddha women will gaze at you with startled looks, glad of your vigour. Rise from this place of damp cane-thickets and fly north, avoiding on your way the rough trunk-blows of the elephants of the quarters. |'},
    {'padas': ['ratnacchāyāvyatikara iva prekṣyametatpurastād', 'valmīkāgrāt prabhavati dhanuḥkhaṇḍamākhaṇḍalasya |', 'yena śyāmaṃ vapuratitarāṃ kāntimāpatsyate te', 'barheṇeva sphuritarucinā gopaveṣasya viṣṇoḥ'], 'num': '|| 15 ||', 'gloss': 'Ahead of you this fragment of Indra’s bow shows itself above an anthill, like a mingling of jewel-lights; through it your dark body will gain great splendour, like Viṣṇu in a herdsman’s dress with a gleaming peacock feather. |'},
    {'padas': ['tvayyāyattaṃ kṛṣiphalamiti bhrūvikārānabhijñaiḥ', 'prītisnigdhairjanapadavadhūlocanaiḥ pīyamānaḥ |', 'sadyaḥsīrotkaṣaṇasurabhi kṣetramāruhya mālaṃ', 'kiṃcitpaścād vraja laghugatirbhūya evottareṇa'], 'num': '|| 16 ||', 'gloss': '“The fruit of the ploughing depends on you” — so think the country-women, who know nothing of the play of brows, and drink you in with eyes soft with affection. Climb the upland field, fragrant with fresh ploughing, go a little westward, and then quickly north again. |'},
    {'padas': ['tvāmāsārapraśamitavanopaplavaṃ sādhu mūrdhnā', 'vakṣyatyadhvaśramaparigataṃ sānumānāmrakūṭaḥ |', "na kṣudro'pi prathamasukṛtāpekṣayā saṃśrayāya", 'prāpte mitre bhavati vimukhaḥ kiṃ punaryastathoccaiḥ'], 'num': '|| 17 ||', 'gloss': 'Mount Āmrakūṭa, whose forest-fires you have quenched with your showers, will bear you, weary from the road, gladly on his head. Even a mean man, remembering an earlier kindness, does not turn his face from a friend who comes for shelter; how much less one so lofty. |'},
    {'padas': ['channopāntaḥ pariṇataphaladyotibhiḥ kānanāmrais-', 'tvayyārūḍhe śikharamacalaḥ snigdhaveṇīsavarṇe |', 'nūnaṃ yāsyatyamaramithunaprekṣaṇīyāmavasthām', 'madhye śyāmaḥ stana iva bhuvaḥ śeṣavistārapāṇḍuḥ'], 'num': '|| 18 ||', 'gloss': 'When you climb his peak, glossy like a braid of hair, with its slopes thick with wild mangoes gleaming ripe, the mountain, dark in the middle and pale all around, will surely look like the breast of the earth — a sight for divine couples. |'},
    {'padas': ['sthitvā tasmin vanacaravadhūbhuktakuñje muhūrtam', 'toyotsargadrutataragatistatparaṃ vartma tīrṇaḥ |', 'revāṃ drakṣyasyupalaviṣame vindhyapāde viśīrṇāṃ', 'bhakticchedairiva viracitāṃ bhūtimaṅge gajasya'], 'num': '|| 19 ||', 'gloss': 'Rest a moment in that grove, enjoyed by forest-women, and then, going faster for having shed your water, pass on along the road. You will see the Revā, scattered over the rocky foot of the Vindhya, like painted streaks of ornament on an elephant’s body. |'},
    {'padas': ['adhvaklāntaṃ pratimukhagataṃ sānumānāmrakūṭas-', 'tuṅgena tvāṃ jalada śirasā vakṣyati ślāghamānaḥ |', 'āsāreṇa tvamapi śamaye tasya naidāghamagniṃ', 'sadbhāvārdraḥ phalati na cireṇopakāro mahatsu'], 'num': '|| 19a ||', 'gloss': 'Weary from the road, Āmrakūṭa, when you come to meet him, will praise you with his lofty head, O cloud. You in turn will quench his summer fire with a downpour; a kindness to the great, moist with goodwill, bears fruit before long. |'},
    {'padas': ['tasyāstiktairvanagajamadairvāsitaṃ vāntavṛṣṭir-', 'jambūkuñjapratihatarayaṃ toyamādāya gaccheḥ |', 'antaḥsāraṃ ghana tulayituṃ nānilaḥ śakṣyati tvāṃ', 'riktaḥ sarvo bhavati hi laghuḥ pūrṇatā gauravāya'], 'num': '|| 20 ||', 'gloss': 'Take up her water, scented with the bitter rut-juice of wild elephants, and go on, your rain spent and your speed checked by the rose-apple thickets. The wind will not be able to lift you, cloud, with that water inside you; emptiness makes everything light, fullness gives weight. |'},
    {'padas': ['nīpaṃ dṛṣṭvā haritakapiśaṃ kesarairardharūḍhair-', 'āvirbhūtaprathamamukulāḥ kandalīścānukaccham |', 'jagdhvāraṇyeṣvadhikasurabhiṃ gandhamāghrāya corvyāḥ', 'sāraṅgāste jalalavamucaḥ sūcayiṣyanti mārgam'], 'num': '|| 21 ||', 'gloss': 'Seeing the kadamba, green and tawny with half-grown filaments, and the plantains opening their first buds along the bank, grazing in the forests and breathing the strong scent of the earth, the deer will point out your path as you let fall your drops. |'},
    {'padas': ['ambhobindugrahaṇacaturāṃścātakān vīkṣamāṇāḥ', 'śreṇībhūtāḥ parigaṇanayā nirdiśanto balākāḥ |', 'tvāmāsādya stanitasamaye mānayiṣyanti siddhāḥ', 'sotkampāni priyasahacarīsambhramāliṅgitāni'], 'num': '|| 22 ||', 'gloss': 'When you arrive, at the hour of thunder, the Siddhas will honour you, watching the cātakas skilled at catching drops of water and the cranes forming lines as if counting; their dear companions, startled, will cling to them, trembling. |'},
    {'padas': ['utpaśyāmi drutamapi sakhe matpriyārthaṃ yiyāsoḥ', 'kālakṣepaṃ kakubhasurabhau parvate parvete te |', 'śuklāpāṅgaiḥ sajalanayanaiḥ svāgatīkṛtya kekāḥ', 'pratyudyātaḥ kathamapi bhavān gantumāśu vyavasyet'], 'num': '|| 23 ||', 'gloss': 'Friend, I foresee that, though you are eager to go quickly for my beloved’s sake, you will lose time on the mountain fragrant with kakubha trees. The peacocks will welcome you with their cries, their eyes wet, the corners white; and somehow, though they come out to meet you, you will make up your mind to go quickly on. |'},
    {'padas': ['pāṇḍucchāyopavanavṛtayaḥ ketakaiḥ sūcibhinnair-', 'nīḍārambhairgṛhabalibhujāmākulagrāmacaityāḥ |', 'tvayyāsanne pariṇataphalaśyāmajambūvanāntāḥ', 'sampatsyante katipayadinasthāyihaṃsā daśārṇāḥ'], 'num': '|| 24 ||', 'gloss': 'When you draw near, the Daśārṇa country will change: the garden hedges turn pale with ketaka buds pricked open by their spikes, the village shrines busy with crows building their nests, the edges of the rose-apple groves dark with ripe fruit, and the swans staying but a few days. |'},
    {'padas': ['teṣāṃ dikṣu prathitavidiśālakṣaṇāṃ rājadhānīṃ', 'gatvā sadyaḥ phalamavikalaṃ kāmukatvasya labdhā |', 'tīropāntastanitasubhagaṃ pāsyasi svādu yasmāt', 'sabhrūbhaṅgaṃ mukhamiva payo vetravatyāścalormi'], 'num': '|| 25 ||', 'gloss': 'Going to their capital, known in all directions as Vidiśā, you will at once gain the full fruit of being a lover: you will drink the sweet water of the Vetravatī, which murmurs charmingly at its banks, its waves rippling, like a face with knitted brows. |'},
    {'padas': ['nīcairākhyaṃ girimadhivasestatra viśrāmahetos-', 'tvatsamparkāt pulakitamiva prauḍhapuṣpaiḥ kadambaiḥ |', 'yaḥ puṇyastrīratiparimalodgāribhirnāgarāṇām', 'uddāmāni prathayati śilāveśmabhiryauvanāni'], 'num': '|| 26 ||', 'gloss': 'There, to rest, settle on the hill called Nīcaiḥ, which seems to thrill at your touch with its full-grown kadamba flowers; from its stone chambers breathes the perfume of the pleasures of courtesans, proclaiming the unbridled youth of the townsmen. |'},
    {'padas': ['viśrāntaḥ san vraja vananadītīrajānāṃ niṣiñcann-', 'udyānānāṃ navajalakaṇairyūthikājālakāni |', 'gaṇḍasvedāpanayanarujāklāntakarṇotpalānāṃ', 'chāyādānāt kṣaṇaparicitaḥ puṣpalāvīmukhānām'], 'num': '|| 27 ||', 'gloss': 'Rested, go on, sprinkling with fresh drops the jasmine buds in the gardens along the forest rivers, and, by giving shade for a moment to the faces of the flower-pickers, whose ear-lotuses droop as they wipe the sweat from their cheeks, make a passing acquaintance. |'},
    {'padas': ['vakraḥ panthā yadapi bhavataḥ prasthitasyottarāśāṃ', 'saudhotsaṅgapraṇayavimukho mā sma bhūrujjayinyāḥ |', 'vidyuddāmasphuritacakitaistatra paurāṅganānāṃ', "lolāpāṅgairyadi na ramase locanairvañcito'si"], 'num': '|| 28 ||', 'gloss': 'Though the road is crooked for one setting out to the north, do not be averse to the lap of Ujjayinī’s mansions; if you do not delight in the restless side-glances of the city women, startled by the flash of your lightning-garlands, you are cheated of your due. |'},
    {'padas': ['vīcikṣobhastanitavihagaśreṇikāñcīguṇāyāḥ', 'saṃsarpantyāḥ skhalitasubhagaṃ darśitāvartanābheḥ |', 'nirvindhyāyāḥ pathi bhava rasābhyantaraḥ saṃnipatya', 'strīṇāmādyaṃ praṇayavacanaṃ vibhramo hi priyeṣu'], 'num': '|| 29 ||', 'gloss': 'On the way, alight on the Nirvindhyā, whose girdle is the line of birds crying at the stirring of her waves, who glides on with a charming stumble and shows the whirlpool of her navel; and taste her within: for a woman’s first word of love to her beloved is coquetry. |'},
    {'padas': ['veṇībhūtapratanusalilā tāmatītasya sindhuḥ', 'pāṇḍucchāyātaṭaruhatarubhraṃśibhirjīrṇaparṇaiḥ |', 'saubhāgyaṃ te subhaga virahāvasthayā vyañjayantī', 'kārśyaṃ yena tyajati vidhinā sa tvayaivopapādyaḥ'], 'num': '|| 30 ||', 'gloss': 'The river Sindhu, her thin water drawn into a braid, pale with the old leaves dropped by the trees on her banks, shows through her state of separation how fortunate you are, fortunate one; you must see to it that she loses her thinness. |'},
    {'padas': ['prāpyāvantīnudayanakathākovidagrāmavṛddhān', 'pūrvoddiṣṭāmupasara purīṃ śrīviśālāṃ viśālām |', 'svalpībhūte sucaritaphale svargiṇāṃ gāṃ gatānāṃ', 'śeṣaiḥ puṇyairhṛtamiva divaḥ kāntimatkhaṇḍamekam'], 'num': '|| 31 ||', 'gloss': 'Reaching Avanti, whose village elders are skilled in the tales of Udayana, approach Viśālā, the city I spoke of before, rich in splendour: it is like one shining piece of heaven, brought down by the heaven-dwellers when the fruit of their good deeds had dwindled, with what was left of their merit. |'},
    {'padas': ['dīrghīkurvan paṭu madakalaṃ kūjitaṃ sārasānāṃ', 'pratyūṣeṣu sphuṭitakamalāmodamaitrīkaṣāyaḥ |', 'yatra strīṇāṃ harati surataglānimaṅgānukūlaḥ', 'śiprāvātaḥ priyatama iva prārthanācāṭukāraḥ'], 'num': '|| 32 ||', 'gloss': 'There the wind from the Śiprā, drawing out the clear, sweet, intoxicated cries of the cranes at dawn, rich with the scent of opening lotuses, kindly to the limbs, takes away women’s weariness after love, like a dear lover coaxing with entreaties. |'},
    {'padas': ['hārāṃstārāṃstaralaguṭikān koṭiśaḥ śaṅkhaśuktīḥ', 'śaṣpaśyāmān marakatamaṇīnunmayūkhaprarohān |', 'dṛṣṭvā yasyāṃ vipaṇiracitān vidrumāṇāṃ ca bhaṅgān', 'saṃlakṣyante salilanidhayastoyamātrāvaśeṣāḥ'], 'num': '|| 33 ||', 'gloss': 'There, seeing in the bazaars necklaces, bright pearls by the million, conches and shells, emerald gems green as young grass with sprouting rays, and heaps of coral, one can tell that the oceans are left with nothing but water. |'},
    {'padas': ["pradyotasya priyaduhitaraṃ vatsarājo'tra jahre", 'haimaṃ tāladrumavanamabhūdatra tasyaiva rājñaḥ |', 'atrodbhrāntaḥ kila nalagiriḥ stambhamutpāṭya darpā-', 'dityāgantūn ramayati jano yatra bandhūnabhijñaḥ'], 'num': '|| 34 ||', 'gloss': 'Here the king of the Vatsas carried off Pradyota’s dear daughter; here was that same king’s golden palm-grove; here Nalagiri, they say, broke his post in pride and ran wild — so the people, who know their kin, entertain visiting relatives with tales. |'},
    {'padas': ['jālodgīrṇairupacitavapuḥ keśasaṃskāradhūpai-', 'rbandhuprītyā bhavanaśikhibhirdattanṛtyopahāraḥ |', 'harmyeṣvasyāḥ kusumasurabhiṣvadhvakhedaṃ nayethā', 'lakṣmīṃ paśyaṁllalitavanitāpādarāgāṅkiteṣu'], 'num': '|| 35 ||', 'gloss': 'Your body fed by the hair-perfuming incense that streams out of the windows, and offered a dance by the house-peacocks in their affection for you, pass your journey’s weariness in her mansions, fragrant with flowers, looking at their beauty, marked with the red dye of the lovely women’s footprints. |'},
    {'padas': ['bhartuḥ kaṇṭhacchaviriti gaṇaiḥ sādaraṃ vīkṣyamāṇaḥ', 'puṇyaṃ yāyāstribhuvanagurordhāma caṇḍīśvarasya |', 'dhūtodyānaṃ kuvalayarajogandhibhirgandhavatyā-', 'stoyakrīḍāniratayuvatisnānatiktairmarudbhiḥ'], 'num': '|| 36 ||', 'gloss': 'Looked on with reverence by Śiva’s attendants as “the colour of the Lord’s throat,” go to the holy abode of Caṇḍīśvara, teacher of the three worlds, where the garden is shaken by the winds from the Gandhavatī, fragrant with lotus pollen and bitter with the bathing-perfume of young women playing in the water. |'},
    {'padas': ['apyanyasmiñjaladhara mahākālamāsādya kāle', 'sthātavyaṃ te nayanaviṣayaṃ yāvadatyeti bhānuḥ |', 'kurvan sandhyābalipaṭahatāṃ śūlinaḥ ślāghanīyām', 'āmandrāṇāṃ phalamavikalaṃ lapsyase garjitānām'], 'num': '|| 37 ||', 'gloss': 'Even if you arrive at Mahākāla at another hour, cloud, you should wait until the sun has gone out of sight; by serving as the drum at the twilight worship of the Trident-bearer you will win the full fruit of your deep thunder. |'},
    {'padas': ['pādanyāsaiḥ kvaṇitaraśanāstatra līlāvadhūtai', 'ratnacchāyākhacitavalibhiścāmaraiḥ klāntahastāḥ |', 'veśyāstvatto nakhapadasukhān prāpya varṣāgrabindūn', 'āmokṣyante tvayi madhukaraśreṇidīrghān kaṭākṣān'], 'num': '|| 38 ||', 'gloss': 'There the courtesans, their girdle-bells jingling at the steps of the dance, their hands tired from waving chowries whose handles are inlaid with the sheen of gems, will receive from you the first raindrops, sweet to their nail-marks, and cast on you long glances like lines of bees. |'},
    {'padas': ['paścāduccairbhujataruvanaṃ maṇḍalenābhilīnaḥ', 'sāndhyaṃ tejaḥ pratinavajapāpuṣparaktaṃ dadhānaḥ |', 'nṛttārambhe hara paśupaterārdranāgājinecchāṃ', 'śāntodvegastimitanayanaṃ dṛṣṭabhaktirbhavānyā'], 'num': '|| 39 ||', 'gloss': 'Then, settling in a circle over the forest of uplifted arms, wearing the twilight glow, red as a fresh hibiscus, take away Paśupati’s wish for the wet elephant-hide at the start of his dance, your devotion seen by Bhavānī, her fear quieted, her eyes steady. |'},
    {'padas': ['gacchantīnāṃ ramaṇavasatiṃ yoṣitāṃ tatra naktaṃ', 'ruddhāloke narapatipathe sūcibhedyaistamobhiḥ |', 'saudāmanyā kanakanikaṣasnigdhayā darśayorvīṃ', 'toyotsargastanitamukharo mā ca bhūrviklavāstāḥ'], 'num': '|| 40 ||', 'gloss': 'At night, on the king’s road, where the light is shut out by darkness thick enough to be pierced by a needle, show the way to the women going to their lovers’ houses with a flash of lightning bright as a streak on a gold touchstone; but do not roar and pour down rain — they are easily frightened. |'},
    {'padas': ['tāṃ kasyāṃcid bhavanavalabhau suptapārāvatāyāṃ', 'nītvā rātriṃ ciravilasanātkhinnavidyutkalatraḥ |', 'dṛṣṭe sūrye punarapi bhavān vāhayedadhvaśeṣaṃ', 'mandāyante na khalu suhṛdāmabhyupetārthakṛtyāḥ'], 'num': '|| 41 ||', 'gloss': 'Spend that night, with your lightning-wife worn out by flashing so long, on the roof-terrace of some house where the pigeons sleep, and when the sun is seen again, go on with the rest of the road; those who have undertaken a friend’s business do not dawdle. |'},
    {'padas': ['tasmin kāle nayanasalilaṃ yoṣitāṃ khaṇḍitānāṃ', 'śāntiṃ neyaṃ praṇayibhirato vartma bhānostyajāśu |', "prāleyāstraṃ kamalavadanātso'pi hartuṃ nalinyāḥ", 'pratyāvṛttastvayi kararudhi syādanalpabhyasūyaḥ'], 'num': '|| 42 ||', 'gloss': 'At that hour the tears of women whose lovers have been unfaithful are to be dried by those lovers; so leave the sun’s path quickly. He too returns to wipe the dew from the lotus-pond’s lotus-face, and if you block his rays he will be bitterly angry. |'},
    {'padas': ['gambhīrāyāḥ payasi saritaścetasīva prasanne', "chāyātmā'pi prakṛtisubhago lapsyate te praveśam |", 'tasmādasyāḥ kumudaviśadānyarhasi tvaṃ na dhairyā-', 'nmoghīkartuṃ caṭulaśapharodvartanaprekṣitāni'], 'num': '|| 43 ||', 'gloss': 'Into the water of the Gambhīrā, clear as a mind, your reflection, though only a shadow, will find entry, being naturally lovely; so out of mere firmness you should not make vain her glances, white as lilies, that flash like the leaping of quick fish. |'},
    {'padas': ['tasyāḥ kiṃcitkaradhṛtamiva prāptavānīraśākhaṃ', 'hṛtvā nīlaṃ salilavasanaṃ muktarodhonitambam |', 'prasthānaṃ te kathamapi sakhe lambamānasya bhāvi', 'jñātāsvādo vivṛtajaghanāṃ ko vihātuṃ samarthaḥ'], 'num': '|| 44 ||', 'gloss': 'Take away her blue water-garment, which seems held a little in the hand of the cane-branches at the edge, slipped from the hips of her banks; as you hang over her, your leaving will somehow come hard, friend: who that has known the taste of it could abandon a woman whose thighs are bare? |'},
    {'padas': ['tvanniṣyandocchvasitavasudhāgandhasamparkaramyaḥ', 'srotorandhradhvanitasubhagaṃ dantibhiḥ pīyamānaḥ |', 'nīcairvāsyatyupajigamiṣordevapūrvaṃ giriṃ te', 'śīto vāyuḥ pariṇamayitā kānanodumbarāṇām'], 'num': '|| 45 ||', 'gloss': 'The cool wind, delightful with the scent of earth breathed out under your showers, sweetly sounding in the trunk-holes of the elephants as they drink it, and ripening the wild figs of the forest, will blow gently as you set out toward Devagiri. |'},
    {'padas': ['tatra skandaṃ niyatavasatiṃ puṣpameghīkṛtātmā', 'puṣpāsāraiḥ snapayatu bhavān vyomagaṅgājalārdraiḥ |', 'rakṣāhetornavaśaśibhṛtā vāsavīnāṃ camūnām', 'atyādityaṃ hutavahamukhe saṃbhṛtaṃ taddhi tejaḥ'], 'num': '|| 46 ||', 'gloss': 'There, turning yourself into a cloud of flowers, bathe Skanda, who dwells there always, with showers of blossoms wet with the water of the heavenly Ganges; for that brilliance, greater than the sun’s, was gathered into the mouth of Fire by the moon-crowned god, to guard the armies of Indra. |'},
    {'padas': ['jyotirlekhāvalayi galitaṃ yasya barhaṃ bhavānī', 'putrapremṇā kuvalayadalaprāpi karṇe karoti |', 'dhautāpāṅgaṃ haraśaśirucā pāvakestaṃ mayūraṃ', 'paścādadrigrahaṇagurubhirgarjitairnartayethāḥ'], 'num': '|| 47 ||', 'gloss': 'Afterwards make his peacock dance with your thunder, doubled by the mountain’s caves — the peacock whose fallen feather, ringed with bands of light, Bhavānī in love for her son wears at her ear beside the lotus petal, and whose eye-corners are washed with the glow of Śiva’s moon. |'},
    {'padas': ['ārādhyainaṃ śaravaṇabhavaṃ devamullaṅghitādhvā', 'siddhadvandvairjalakaṇabhayād vīṇibhirmuktamārgaḥ |', 'vyālambethāḥ surabhitanayālambhajāṃ mānayiṣyan', 'srotomūrtyā bhuvi pariṇatāṃ rantidevasya kīrtim'], 'num': '|| 48 ||', 'gloss': 'When you have worshipped the god born in the reeds and gone on, the Siddha couples with their vīṇās leaving your path for fear of your drops, descend to honour the glory of Rantideva, which took shape on earth as a river, born of the sacrifice of cows. |'},
    {'padas': ['tvayyādātuṃ jalamavanate śārṅgiṇo varṇacaure', 'tasyāḥ sindhoḥ pṛthumapi tanuṃ dūrabhāvāt pravāham |', 'prekṣiṣyante gaganagatayo nūnamāvarjya dṛṣṭī-', 'rekaṃ muktāguṇamiva bhuvaḥ sthūlamadhyendranīlam'], 'num': '|| 49 ||', 'gloss': 'When you bend to take up her water, thief of Viṣṇu’s colour, the sky-travellers, lowering their eyes, will surely see her stream, though broad, thin from afar, like a single string of pearls of the earth with a great sapphire in the middle. |'},
    {'padas': ['tāmuttīrya vraja paricitabhrūlatāvibhramāṇāṃ', 'pakṣmotkṣepāduparivilasatkṛṣṇaśāraprabhāṇām |', 'kundakṣepānugamadhukaraśrīmuṣāmātmabimbaṃ', 'pātrīkurvan daśapuravadhūnetrakautūhalānām'], 'num': '|| 50 ||', 'gloss': 'Crossing her, go on, making your own reflection the object of curiosity to the eyes of the women of Daśapura, whose play of brows is well known, whose glances, as the lashes are raised, gleam dark and dappled, and which steal the beauty of bees following a flung jasmine. |'},
    {'padas': ['brahmāvartaṃ janapadamatha cchāyayā gāhamānaḥ', 'kṣetraṃ kṣatrapradhanapiśunaṃ kauravaṃ tad bhajethāḥ |', 'rājanyānāṃ śitaśaraśatairyatra gāṇḍīvadhanvā', 'dhārāpātaistvamiva kamalānyabhyavarṣanmukhāni'], 'num': '|| 51 ||', 'gloss': 'Then, passing in your shadow over the land of Brahmāvarta, visit the field of the Kurus, witness to the battle of the warriors, where the wielder of Gāṇḍīva rained hundreds of sharp arrows on the faces of the kings, as you rain showers on lotuses. |'},
    {'padas': ['hitvā hālāmabhimatarasāṃ revatīlocanāṅkāṃ', 'bandhuprītyā samaravimukho lāṅgalī yāḥ siṣeve |', 'kṛtvā tāsāmadhigamamapāṃ saumya sārasvatīnām', 'antaḥ śuddhastvamapi bhavitā varṇamātreṇa kṛṣṇaḥ'], 'num': '|| 52 ||', 'gloss': 'The plough-bearer, shunning battle out of kindness to his kin, gave up the liquor he loved, marked with the reflection of Revatī’s eyes, and served those waters; go down to the Sarasvatī’s waters, gentle one, and you too will be clean within, dark only in colour. |'},
    {'padas': ['tasmād gaccheranukanakhalaṃ śailarājāvatīrṇāṃ', 'jahnoḥ kanyāṃ sagaratanayasvargasopānapaṅktim |', 'gaurīvaktrabhrukuṭiracanāṃ yā vihasyeva phenaiḥ', 'śambhoḥ keśagrahaṇamakarodindulagnormihastā'], 'num': '|| 53 ||', 'gloss': 'From there go on by Kanakhala to the daughter of Jahnu, who came down from the king of mountains, the stair to heaven for Sagara’s sons; with her foam she seems to laugh at the frown on Gaurī’s face, and with hands of waves clasping the moon she took hold of Śambhu’s hair. |'},
    {'padas': ['tasyāḥ pātuṃ suragaja iva vyomni paścārdhalambī', 'tvaṃ cedacchasphaṭikaviśadaṃ tarkayestiryagambhaḥ |', 'saṃsarpantyā sapadi bhavataḥ srotasi cchāyayāsau', 'syādasthānopagatayamunāsaṅgamevābhirāmā'], 'num': '|| 54 ||', 'gloss': 'If you, hanging with your rear half in the sky like a heavenly elephant bending to drink, should bend slantwise to her water, clear as crystal, then your shadow gliding in her stream will make her lovely as a confluence with the Yamunā in the wrong place. |'},
    {'padas': ['āsīnānāṃ surabhitaśilaṃ nābhigandhairmṛgāṇāṃ', 'tasyā eva prabhavamacalaṃ prāpya gauraṃ tuṣāraiḥ |', 'vakṣyasyadhvaśramavinayane tasya śṛṅge niṣaṇṇaḥ', 'śobhāṃ śubhrāṃ trinayanavṛṣotkhātapaṅkopameyam'], 'num': '|| 55 ||', 'gloss': 'Reaching the mountain that is her source, white with snow, its rocks perfumed by the musk of the deer that rest there, sit on its peak to ease the weariness of the road; you will wear a pure beauty, like the mud tossed up by the bull of the three-eyed god. |'},
    {'padas': ['taṃ ced vāyau sarati saralaskandhasaṃghaṭṭajanmā', 'bādhetolkākṣapitacamarībālabhāro davāgniḥ |', 'arhasyenaṃ śamayitumalaṃ vāridhārāsahasrai-', 'rāpannārtipraśamanaphalāḥ saṃpado hyuttamānām'], 'num': '|| 56 ||', 'gloss': 'If a forest fire, born of the rubbing of pine trunks together, should spread in the wind and scorch the tail-hairs of the yaks with its sparks, you are fit to put it out with thousands of streams of water; the riches of the great are for relieving the distress of those in trouble. |'},
    {'padas': ['ye saṃrambhotpatanarabhasāḥ svāṅgabhaṅgāya tasmin', 'muktādhvānaṃ sapadi śarabhā laṅghayeyurbhavantam |', 'tān kurvīthāstumulakarakāvṛṣṭipātāvakīrṇān', 'ke vā na syuḥ paribhavapadaṃ niṣphalārambhayatnāḥ'], 'num': '|| 57 ||', 'gloss': 'The śarabhas that leap up in rage to break their own limbs on you, leaving your path, you should scatter at once with falling storms of hail; who does not become an object of scorn when his efforts are vain? |'},
    {'padas': ['tatra vyaktaṃ dṛṣadi caraṇanyāsamardhendumauleḥ', 'śaśvat siddhairupacitabaliṃ bhaktinamraḥ parīyāḥ |', 'yasmin dṛṣṭe karaṇavigamādūrdhvamuddhūtapāpāḥ', 'kalpiṣyante sthiragaṇapadaprāptaye śraddadhānāḥ'], 'num': '|| 58 ||', 'gloss': 'There, bowed in devotion, circle the footprint of the half-moon-crowned god, clearly seen on the rock and ever honoured with offerings by the Siddhas; seeing it, the faithful, their sins shaken off and their bodies laid down, are made fit to attain a firm place among Śiva’s hosts. |'},
    {'padas': ['śabdāyante madhuramanilaiḥ kīcakāḥ pūryamāṇāḥ', 'saṃraktābhistripuravijayo gīyate kiṃnarābhiḥ |', 'nirhrādaste muraja iva cet kandareṣu dhvaniḥ syāt', 'saṃgītārtho nanu paśupatestatra bhāvī samagraḥ'], 'num': '|| 59 ||', 'gloss': 'The bamboos, filled by the wind, sound sweetly; Kinnara women, moved by love, sing the victory over Tripura; if your thunder in the caves should sound like a drum, the whole concert for Paśupati’s worship will be there. |'},
    {'padas': ['prāleyādrerupataṭamatikramya tāṃstān viśeṣān', 'haṃsadvāraṃ bhṛgupatiyaśovartma yat krauñcarandhram |', 'tenodīcīṃ diśamanusarestiryagāyāmaśobhī', 'śyāmaḥ pādo baliniyamanābhyudyatasyeva viṣṇoḥ'], 'num': '|| 60 ||', 'gloss': 'Having passed the various sights along the slopes of the Snow Mountain, go by the Swan-gate, the Krauñca pass, the road of Paraśurāma’s fame; take it northward, beautiful in your slanting length, dark like the foot of Viṣṇu raised to bind Bali. |'},
    {'padas': ['gatvā cordhvaṃ daśamukhabhujocchvāsitaprasthasandheḥ', 'kailāsasya tridaśavanitādarpaṇasyātithiḥ syāḥ |', 'śṛṅgocchrāyaiḥ kumudaviśadairyo vitatya sthitaḥ khaṃ', 'rāśībhūtaḥ pratidinamiva tryambakasyāṭṭahāsaḥ'], 'num': '|| 61 ||', 'gloss': 'Going higher, you will be a guest of Kailāsa, the mirror of the heavenly women, whose base-joints were loosened by the arms of the ten-headed demon; it stands, spreading across the sky with peaks white as lilies, like the loud laughter of the three-eyed god piled up day after day. |'},
    {'padas': ['utpaśyāmi tvayi taṭagate snigdhabhinnāñjanābhe', 'sadyaḥ kṛttadviradadaśanacchedagaurasya tasya |', 'śobhāmadreḥ stimitanayanaprekṣaṇīyāṃ bhavitrīm', 'aṃsanyaste sati halabhṛto mecake vāsasīva'], 'num': '|| 62 ||', 'gloss': 'I imagine that when you rest on its slope, glossy as split collyrium, the mountain, white as a tusk freshly cut, will have a beauty to gaze at unblinking, like a dark robe laid on the shoulder of the plough-bearer. |'},
    {'padas': ['hitvā tasmin bhujagavalayaṃ śambhunā dattahastā', 'krīḍāśaile yadi ca vicaretpādacāreṇa gaurī |', 'bhaṅgībhaktyā viracitavapuḥ stambhitāntarjalaughaḥ', 'sopānatvaṃ kuru maṇitaṭārohaṇāyāgrayāyī'], 'num': '|| 63 ||', 'gloss': 'If Gaurī, her hand in Śambhu’s, he having put aside his serpent bracelet, should walk on foot on that pleasure-mountain, then make your body a stair, your inner waters stilled in ripples, and go before her, that she may climb the jewelled slope. |'},
    {'padas': ['tatrāvaśyaṃ valayakuliśodghaṭṭanodgīrṇatoyaṃ', 'neṣyanti tvāṃ surayuvatayo yantradhārāgṛhatvam |', 'tābhyo mokṣastava yadi sakhe gharmalabdhasya na syāt', 'krīḍālolāḥ śravaṇaparuṣairgarjitairbhāyayestāḥ'], 'num': '|| 64 ||', 'gloss': 'There the young women of the gods will surely use you as a shower-house, striking you with their diamond bracelets so the water pours out; if you cannot escape them, friend, caught in the heat, frighten those playful girls with harsh thunder, grating to the ear. |'},
    {'padas': ['hemāmbhojaprasavi salilaṃ mānasasyādadānaḥ', 'kurvan kāmaṃ kṣaṇamukhapaṭaprītimairāvatasya |', 'dhunvan kalpadrumakisalayānyaṃśukānīva vātai-', 'rnānāceṣṭairjaladalalitairnirviśestaṃ nagendram'], 'num': '|| 65 ||', 'gloss': 'Taking the water of Mānasa, which bears golden lotuses, giving Airāvata for a moment the pleasure of a veil over his face, shaking the leaves of the wishing-trees like garments in your winds, enjoy that king of mountains with all the playful ways of a cloud. |'},
    {'padas': ['tasyotsaṅge praṇayina iva srastagaṅgādukūlāṃ', 'na tvaṃ dṛṣṭvā na punaralakāṃ jñāsyase kāmacārin |', 'yā vaḥ kāle vahati salilodgāramuccairvimānā', 'muktājālagrathitamalakaṃ kāminīvābhravṛndam'], 'num': '|| 66 ||', 'gloss': 'Seeing her in his lap, like a lover with the Ganges as her slipped silken robe, you, who go as you please, will surely know Alakā — she who in the season bears masses of water in her lofty mansions, as a woman bears her hair strung with nets of pearls, a mass of clouds. |'},
    ],
}
